.gradle/
build/
# candor's own analysis output. `.candor/policy` is an INPUT and stays tracked; the report and its
# sidecars are generated, so ignore those by name rather than the whole directory (candor-rust draws the
# same line, for the same reason). Left untracked, a scan run in this repo makes `git status --porcelain`
# non-empty, and both `release-stage.sh` and `release.sh` step 0 refuse on that — so a stray report from
# investigating a defect blocks the release that fixes it. candor-ts, candor-swift and candor-agents all
# ignore theirs; this repo was the outlier.
.candor/report.*
.candor/*.scan.json
.candor/*.callgraph.json
.candor/*.hierarchy.json
.DS_Store
# scratchpad/ is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — see CLAUDE.md. A read-only agent once left 203 MB
# inside a repo because its brief gave a RELATIVE scratch path, and `git status` showing
# `?? scratchpad/` is what caught it. This line existed until 2026-09-26 and 240 MB had
# accumulated behind it, cited by no register row. Agents get the ABSOLUTE session path instead.
